Snapshot the aerosol state after each of the thirteen process calls.

ukca_aero_step calls thirteen process routines per chemistry step. Comparing
only the end state tells you THAT a port diverged; comparing after each call
tells you WHERE. Budgets carry mass fluxes only -- no nd, no mdt, no drydp --
so they cannot localise the failures that actually happen in coagulation and
mode merging, which is why this exists alongside 0002 rather than instead of it.

Records are long-format: one line per (step, site, imts, izts, field, mode,
component, value) at ES24.16. Verbose, but it makes any diff attributable to a
single array element.

Instrumentation only. Every hunk touching src/ukca/ is an INSERTION -- the
build script rejects any patch that removes a line from a UKCA file, because a
removal is a science change wearing instrumentation's clothes. The dump module
itself lives in src/box/ (new BSD-3 code) and deliberately has no USE
statements, so calling it from src/ukca cannot create a dependency cycle with
the box modules that already depend on UKCA.

Controlled by state_file in &box_run; empty means not written.

